  "findings": [
    "The previous Web rule uniformly scaled the 1800px master below 1800px, shrinking all event text and artwork on common desktop widths.",
    "v44 lays out the calendar at the available desktop width from 1000px through 1799px while retaining the governed font sizes and no horizontal overflow.",
    "At 999px and below the Web artifact preserves its 1800px layout width and applies one zoom factor, filling the viewport without the former flex-shrink plus transform double contraction.",
    "Every calendar-cell promotion is measured inside its cell and against its venue/time anchors at each viewport; the private title, location, time and date badge are also checked for containment and collision.",
    "The public Wix page currently exposes the approved September v12 as a Wix-hosted 1800x1204 image record and also stores its review URL; customer readability therefore depends on the Wix component/container fit, not only the source bitmap dimensions."
  ],
